WEBVTT

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.920
I got your paperwork, Dr. Fleischman.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.160
Oh, hey, yeah, thank you.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.180
Just put it right down there.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:14.720
Thank you.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.440
Your dad says I can help you some more, too.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:18.660
Well, if it's truly important.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.010
Important?

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.780
Well, John Hopkins School of Medicine is behind this clinical study.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.860
Is that important enough for you?

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.790
This is John Hopkins, as in sorry, Mr. Fleischman.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.330
Plebeians need not apply here.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:35.900
Check this out. Some of the same people who turned me down for med school happened to be on the committee that chose Sicily for this particular study.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.220
I mean, they could have chose a hundred other towns, right?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.560
I mean, they could have chose any other town, but they chose this one. Why?

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.730
And I'll tell you why. Because of my exhaustive database, that's why.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.280
So can, uh, these things really keep you from getting a cold?

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.060
Well, I mean, we don't know that. That's why we're running a test.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:58.250
So half the town will get the medication, half will get the placebo, and then we'll see if there's any statistical differences.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:00:58.970
That'll tell us.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.510
Oh, very tricky.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:02.140
Yeah.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.780
So who gets the real ones?

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:04.890
Look at the draw.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.260
All right, look, here's what I need you to do.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.820
First, just put the caps on top of the vials, all right?

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.560
Marilyn's uncle threw a rod.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.400
It's four-by, actually, so I'm gonna go pick her up, all right?

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.120
Just don't let anyone near those pills.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.490
Sure thing, Dr. Fleischman.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:19.270
Thanks, Ed.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.140
Follow me. You're not supposed to be in here.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.360
Come here. Come here.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.700
Thank you.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:30.430
on.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.380
Rise and shine all UK bear ptarmigan heads.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.680
Chris here with the breakfast waffles.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.570
Message of the day, every coin has at least two sides

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:12.870
behind every great pro.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:16.070
Look for the con, yin and yang, another man's meat,

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.390
blah, blah, blah, you know the drill.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.340
At least some of us are gonna be spared the indignities

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.600
of another cold season.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.400
Billboard alert, Dr. Joel and his able assistant Marilyn

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.660
are gonna be dispensing a new experimental medication

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.500
which promises to help slay that

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.820
multi-armed Hydra we've come to know as the common cold.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.850
Just hope you're not one of the 50% of the volunteers

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.420
who is gonna end up shooting blanks.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:41.550
I wanna introduce a very special friend of mine.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.170
Ladies and gentlemen, give it up for Esau.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:45.860
Thanks, Chris.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.730
I appreciate the chance to do the Kathy Lee thing

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:49.490
with you this week.

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.370
I should explain to my K-Bear audience

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.840
that Esau's a dummy.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.190
Well, I say that without a hint of derisiveness.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:59.790
Term of choice these days, Chris, is wooden American.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.520
But I'm comfortable with dummy.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.420
I picked up you saw on a recent trip to Fairbanks in a toy store.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.720
I couldn't resist that cherubic smile,

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:12.540
the old soul behind those twinkling azure eyes,

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.080
the 40% markdown.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.040
Relax, Chris. You're pressing.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.620
All right, I know what you're thinking.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.780
Ventriloquism on the radio.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.980
It's just a cut above pantomime and close-up magic

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.660
in the kit bag of useless skills, right?

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.970
Fact is, it's one of Chris's few, if not only now.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:33.590
something he's been binding to do for years.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.670
Yeah, it's good to see a ventriloquist

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.250
acted ahead and go straight for the wood jokes.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.860
Yeah, what can I say? They go against my grain.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:40.280
Okay.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.550
But I would like to take issue just a tad

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.890
with all that yin-yang, life's a coin toss stuff.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.700
I don't buy it for a minute.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.340
You don't?

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:50.800
Golly, no, Chris.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.820
The way I see it, there's the truth, there are lies.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.650
There's messing up, and there's doing the right thing.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.970
Well, that might work for a wooden...

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.000
but I, for one, am leery of moral compasses.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.280
I mean, absolutes.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.960
At the end of the day, who are we to judge?

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:10.320
We're human, that's what. You are, anyway.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.660
And, gosh, what could be more human than making judgments

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.020
and sticking by your guns?

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.690
Well, I think what's human is seeing life in all its confounding complexity,

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.290
raising up your hands and saying,

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.210
hey, there might not be any answers.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.000
Crass, crass, crass, crass, crass, crass, crass.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.420
I was winning alongside someone a lot like you.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.750
Talk about the chronically indecisive.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.220
This blockhead still thinks the jury's out on beta versus VHS.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:36.300
20 minutes with the sap, you're ready to give him a good shellacking.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.480
Okay, these are your pills for the first 20-day cycle.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.760
Just take one every morning, okay?

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:47.090
No, is that on an empty stomach or having head?

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.300
Best always to eat something, yeah.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.240
Yeah, what kind of wine we got out there?

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.220
Oh, it's thinning.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.910
Dr. Fleischman, I was wondering.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.730
Don't worry, you're temporary staff.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.430
No, I can't tell you.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.020
Well, what I was wondering is...

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:08.150
two of our patients switched medications.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.240
Well, could that... would that be toxic?

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.540
No, no, definitely not.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:16.110
Good.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:20.350
I mean, it would certainly invalidate them from the study.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.870
A sample this size, a couple of instances like that...

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.600
would definitely skew the results. Why?

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:29.960
Oh, nothing. I was just wondering...

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:33.390
Thanks for the pills.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.920
I guess inviting a man to our woman's group does require a little explanation.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:43.000
Um, everyone, this is Roger Brewster.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.740
Now, I'm, like, the last one to go for something like this.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.250
But after I tried his product, I just had to share it with the rest of you, right?

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.730
Well, you're not alone, Maggie.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:54.350
Over a quarter million sold in North America alone.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:55.290
Right.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.980
So, before we get down to Jean, Shinoda Boland's goddesses and every woman...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.400
I thought perhaps, you know, he could make his presentation.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:04.890
Sorry, guys.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:07.970
Miranda went through the last of the clean diaps.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.410
Had to run out for disposables.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:10.870
And who might this be?

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:11.710
Me.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.150
Might be Shelly Tambo-Vincore.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.770
Thought we were gonna talk about goddess stuff.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:19.410
Roger's a salesman.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:21.050
What are you selling?

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:22.030
Me?

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.740
I like to call it the one-hour vacation.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.650
He sells jacuzzis.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:27.790
Whirlpools, actually.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:29.280
Jacuzzi's a trade name.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:29.980
And my...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.750
units pack more wallop, bubble for bubble. Seriously, let me ask you all something. What's

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:42.960
the number one killer in the world today? Famine. Actually, I was thinking of stress.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:51.160
Tension literally melts away. Shelly, you look like a show me kind of gal. I do. Come

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:56.000
on now, don't be shy. Our hostess, Ms. O'Connell, has graciously allowed me to set up one of

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.230
the units in her tub. Shall we?

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.300
Ladies, I give you the InstaSpa, model 2000.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.590
You're looking at 1.5 horses,

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:13.030
Norton through 710 strategically placed therapeutic pinholes,

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.450
lockdown handrails, Roman pillow,

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.950
dial-of-flow jets, topside controls,

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.320
a personal paradise for one.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.140
Isn't it perfect?

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.640
It's like a hot tub with all that boring conversation.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.040
Shelly, why don't you stick your feet in there?

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.140
Come on.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:28.360
Go on, tell us how it feels.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.500
That a girl, now don't be shy.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:42.110
Looks like you've died and gone to heaven, isn't it?

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.570
Sprinkle in a few scented granules,

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:46.310
deliciously reminiscent of Giorgio,

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.360
and tell the world to take a hike.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.080
Now, whether you order one or not,

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.440
I would like you all to take with you

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:58.100
a complimentary basket of personal care products

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.970
courtesy of me...

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.340
And InstaSpot.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:06.780
Ah, it looks like I'm one short.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.300
Hey, no big.

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:10.340
No, Shelly.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:13.520
I'm gonna have to come up with something extra special for you.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:19.580
Hello, Joel.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:20.590
Hey, Maurice.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:20.930
How you doing?

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.460
Nice cover story.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:29.190
You know, that common cold gambit makes the results all the more valid when they start flooding in, right?

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:29.690
What?

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.100
Come on, Joel. I'm not a child.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:38.570
I mean, you know, and I know, that that coal business is a lot of hooey.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:39.990
Why don't we call it what it is?

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:42.000
You want data? I'll give you data.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:47.120
Last night at 2300, I made my usual trek down to the Sub-Zero.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:53.580
But, instead of nuking yakitori appetizer and then following that up with a bowl of Cherry Garcia,

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.610
I went for a humble pippin.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:59.640
And then this morning at the brick, I even passed by genuine...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.920
Vermont Maple. So what you're trying to tell me is that you think the pills have some kind of

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:10.340
appetite suppressant in them. Joel, I know there's an appetite suppressant. I just thought you might

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:16.540
like to share the particulars with me. I can't tell you whether or not you're even on the medication,

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:21.470
okay? Now, I will certainly note the side effects for the record, but that's all I can and will do.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:29.230
What am I talking about? I know you've got confidences to keep.

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.970
Just, uh, give me the name, okay?

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.600
Look, please, all right? No offense.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.300
I have a conference call to Baltimore,

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.940
and I really should be prepping for it, okay?

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:45.630
Refreshing to see a man stand by the code,

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:46.550
even under pressure.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:49.530
Shows moxie.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:06.640
Hi there, Shelly.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:08.360
Oh, it's you.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:09.660
I brought you something.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.300
Black Sabbath, bootleg.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.340
Recorded it myself at the Cow Palace.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.160
I'm a humongous Sabbath fan.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:17.820
How'd you know?

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:18.940
I'm a salesman.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.720
I make my living reading people.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:21.700
Mind if I come in?

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.280
I hope you've got Dolby, though, on your tape deck.

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:26.280
There's some hiss on that.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:27.580
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:28.680
I got to 86 you.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:29.980
I got a gazillion things to do.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.880
Oh, I thought maybe we could just talk for a minute.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:33.810
Look, Mr. Brewster.

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:34.570
Roger.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.470
You know, a woman like you can really bring out the devil in a man.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:41.800
Hey, watch it, dude.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.080
Sorry, that was inexcusable.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.260
Sorry doesn't cut it.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:47.300
My squeeze is right there in the shower.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:48.880
And even if he wasn't.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:49.700
Shelly, I'm sorry.

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:50.080
Out.

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:51.970
You heard me.

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:53.030
Beat it.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:12:59.970
So, Ed, how do you like?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.160
them Ivy League speedballs.

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:01.960
What?

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.560
You know, the experimental pills from John Hopkins.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.000
Hollings says that Maurice says

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.240
there's some kind of a stimulant.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:08.150
Oh.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:10.050
All I know is I split enough wood

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.570
to fill half a rail car this morning.

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:12.730
My pecs aren't even sore.

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.640
Hi, fellas. How's it hanging?

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:20.680
Something wrong, eh?

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.210
I don't know. I just got a bit of an arctic blast.

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:26.080
You know, hoppers can do that.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.580
It cuts off the blood to your toes.

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:28.660
Huh.

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:32.030
If you gentlemen will excuse me.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:40.100
Shelly, just give me two seconds.

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:43.160
Why don't you go soak your head in one of your tugs?

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.600
I blew it. Okay. I just want to make it right.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.400
Hit the road, Jack.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:48.980
That's how you can make it right.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.600
Just tell me your biggest fantasy.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.020
Get a new line, will ya?

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.760
No, not that kind of fantasy.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:56.170
Come on, really.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.700
What would make you happier than anything else in the world?

00:13:58.920 --> 00:13:59.980
You just don't know when to...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:07.370
do you? Your heart's dream, what would it be? Come on, Shelly, please. If I tell you, will you get

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:17.280
out of my face? Hey, Scott's on. Ultima fantasy. No holds barred, no fine print. Big universe out

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:23.720
there, Shelly, and it's all at your command. So what'll it be? Eternal youth, the ability to

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:29.970
become invisible, power beyond reckoning. I wish the state of Alaska would legalize

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:35.340
gambling like Las Vegas you know and the Brit would become this heavy-duty casino

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:55.120
this place a casino okay works for me look at that well well well opportunity

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:59.890
knocks you seen the news out of Claywalk Claywalk a local

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.320
Well, Tlingit leader just got the state to sanction lower 48 casino-style gambling.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.950
First crack in the damn wall.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:08.430
What's that got to do with you?

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.450
Well, my attorney in Anchorage used to be a member of the New Jersey Gaming Commission.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:19.060
According to him, the borough of Arrowhead could qualify for a gambling exemption under Title 20.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:20.460
Legalized gambling?

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.510
Yeah, a man can hope, can't he?

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.690
Okay, thank you, caller.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.970
It's amazing how you tied up Marv's problems of...

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.800
and Helen's issues of narcissism

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:36.600
into a M. Scott Peck Jiminy Cricket Ragu kind of a thing.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:37.760
How do you do that, Esau?

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.880
I've got the easy job, Chris. I speak from the heart.

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:43.580
You're the one who has to take that treacherous detour

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.660
through the superego.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:48.630
Well, okay. Next caller,

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:50.830
you're on the air with Chris and Esau in the morning.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:52.590
Hi, Chris. Connie Grippo.

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.070
Hey, Connie. What's up?

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:55.670
You know, Esau, how you were saying,

